WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:02.600
Good morning, Hank; it's Wednesday. Who am
I kidding? You're not watching this; you're

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:03.600
in Haiti!

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.070
Hank, I'm really grateful to you for being
the noble brother who goes out there on the

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:11.920
front lines to decrease WorldSuck because
that means that I can stay in my basement.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.200
Why am I still talking to him? He's not watching!

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.580
We are free from the tyranny of Hank!

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:19.340
Okay, nerdfighters. This morning I went to
Your Pants and asked for some questions and

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.090
now... here are some answers!

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:24.010
"After reading 'Looking for Alaska,' I wonder
if you've thought about what you want your

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:25.600
last words to be before you die."

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:30.150
Not at all. To paraphrase the great John Barrymore,
"dying is the last thing I would ever do."

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.970
"Did you have any nicknames as a teenager?"

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:35.590
Yeah, one time I said that Christian Slater
never made a bad more and, thereafter, a lot

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:37.340
of my friends called me "Kuffs."

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:40.050
"Dandy lions or dandelions?"

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:43.770
Oh, dandy lions for sure. Do you know what
happens if you wish on a dandy lion?

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:44.770
He eats you.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:47.160
By the way, "The Dandy Lions"... really good
band name.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.969
"It's tax time again. Any fishing boat proceeds
this year?"

00:00:49.969 --> 00:00:53.649
No. Stupid fishing boats always refusing to
give me proceeds.

00:00:53.649 --> 00:00:54.780
"When's your new book coming out?"

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.500
In almost exactly one year.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.500
"What's it about?"

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:01.170
Uh, it's about these two teenage cancer survivors
who are both obsessed with this reclusive

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:04.370
novelist, but it's also about a bunch of other
things like Swedish hip-hop and, you know,

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:05.619
the meaning of life and stuff.

00:01:05.619 --> 00:01:07.240
"Is it really narrated by a girl?"

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:08.380
Yes! Hazel!

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:09.399
"What's the title?"

00:01:09.399 --> 00:01:12.630
I don't know! I change it, like, every day
and they all suck!

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:15.700
Do you have any good titles? If you have any
good titles, please leave them in comments!

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:19.299
"What is the biggest obstacle, in your opinion,
to getting started as a professional writer?"

00:01:19.299 --> 00:01:24.009
Um, essentially, the world contains a lot
of books and not that many people who are

00:01:24.009 --> 00:01:25.439
willing to pay to read them.

00:01:25.439 --> 00:01:27.840
"Can you say the alphabet backwards?"

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.539
Z, Y, X, W... no.

00:01:29.539 --> 00:01:32.759
"Are you friends with Libba Bray? Have you
read any of her books?"

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:36.590
Yes, I'm friends with Libba Bray, and I've
read all of her books, including "Beauty Queens,"

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:37.590
which isn't even out yet.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:41.159
Did you know that Libba Bray just broke both
of her elbows? I realize that sounds like

00:01:41.159 --> 00:01:44.399
a euphemism for being pregnant with twins
or something, but seriously, Libba Bray just

00:01:44.399 --> 00:01:45.429
broke both of her elbows.

00:01:45.429 --> 00:01:48.489
And I'm not even that surprised about it,
to be honest. Like, if you told me, "John,

00:01:48.489 --> 00:01:53.179
one of your friends just broke both of her
elbows," I would be, like, "I bet it was Libba!"

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:56.090
You never here about people like Sarah Dessen
breaking both of their elbows. It just doesn't

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:59.819
happen. Poor Libba. Anyway, her new book is
amazing; you should preorder it — link in

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:04.030
the dooblydoo. I didn't end up writing a desert
island novel because, you know, after Libba's,

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:05.030
I don't have to.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:06.270
"Will you ever walk alone?"

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:07.270
No!

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:09.459
And if I didn't know this was a Liverpool
scarf, I might think I was dressing up as

00:02:09.459 --> 00:02:10.530
Waldo for Christmas.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:14.219
[to self] You don't dress up for Christmas,
Green. Get your head outta your ass.

00:02:14.219 --> 00:02:17.299
"Hey, is your phone number secretly inserted
into 'Looking for Alaska'?"

00:02:17.299 --> 00:02:20.900
Yeah... that used to be my phone number. I
mean, when I wrote "Looking for Alaska," I

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:25.190
didn't think more than about nine people would
read it, you know, so yes, I did put my phone

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:26.190
number in it.

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:30.079
I have a message for the person who has that
phone number now: Sorry.

00:02:30.079 --> 00:02:31.920
"Favorite old-school video game?"

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:35.750
Pong, because I like video games that are
like life and Pong just keeps getting harder

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:36.870
until you die.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.170
"Have you ever been arrested?"

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.170
No.

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:41.719
"Coffee or tea?"

00:02:41.719 --> 00:02:44.030
Coffee. I'm hiding from the British people.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.590
"If you could, would you?"

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:49.010
Probably not. Let's face it: I'm not the kinda
guy who does.

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:52.209
Hank, thank you for going to Haiti. We look
forward to the most amazing Thoughts from

00:02:52.209 --> 00:02:56.849
Places videos ever, and I will see you on
Friday when I upload the video that you already

00:02:56.849 --> 00:02:57.849
made.

00:02:57.849 --> 00:03:03.840
But I will really see you on... I'm so bad
at this... Wednesday? It seems so far away.

